# Footnotes (reference/components/footnote.md). Pages of 300 × 200 with margins of 20: page area of 260 × 160 from
# (20, 20), which ends at y = 180. Lines of 12 (Size 10); at 5 pt per character, 52 characters fit per line. The
# footnote area has, by default, a top margin of 8, a rule of 0.5 and a padding of 4 above its notes: 12.5 more than
# the notes, with the rule 8 below the text that precedes it.
#
# Section 1: p1 calls a and p2 calls b and c on the same line; tall (100) and p3, which calls d, follow. With the four
#   notes (48 + 12.5 = 60.5) the page leaves 99.5 and tall does not fit: it moves to page 2 with p3, and the page
#   reserves the three notes it calls (36 + 12.5 = 48.5): the area, 40.5 high, at 139.5; a at 144, b at 156, c at 168.
# Page 2: tall at 20 and p3 at 120, with d below: area of 16.5 at 163.5, d at 168.
# Section 2: the numbering starts again in letters. big (60) and p5, which calls e, 8 lines (96). The three together
#   (60 + 12 + 108.5) exceed 160, so p5 moves to page 4 with its note, and page 3 only has big. Page 4: p5 at 20 and the
#   area, 100.5 high, at 79.5, with e at 84.
# Section 3: q1, 10 lines, calls f, 12 lines (144), in its first line; q2, 10 lines, follows. f does not fit under its
#   line even alone: only its first 10 lines do (148 reserved: a line of q1 at the top, and 135.5 for the notes, where
#   11 lines fit but the last two go together). Page 5: q1's first line at 20, the area at 55.5 (124.5 high) with f's
#   10 lines at 60. Page 6: the end of f (2 lines) comes first in the area, and q1's other 9 lines (108) fit above it:
#   q1 at 20, area of 28.5 at 151.5, f at 156. q2 does not fit (one line would violate orphans) and goes to page 7.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Markup: markdown
	Section:
		Paragraph: Uno[^a] dos.
			Id: p1
		Paragraph: Tres[^b] cuatro[^c].
			Id: p2
		Footnote:
			Id: a
			Paragraph: Nota a.
		Footnote:
			Id: b
			Paragraph: Nota b.
		Block:
			Id: tall
			Box:
				Height: 100
			Break:
				Keep together: true
		Paragraph: Cinco[^d].
			Id: p3
		Footnote:
			Id: c
			Paragraph: Nota c.
		Footnote:
			Id: d
			Paragraph: Nota d.
	Section:
		Footnote numbering: restart
		Footnote number format: lower-alpha
		Block:
			Id: big
			Box:
				Height: 60
		Paragraph: Seis[^e].
			Id: p5
